course: dictionary
lesson: 15420
title: Steady words: stabilising
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word stabilising comes from stable, which means steady and firm. To stabilise something is to make it steady, so it does not wobble, fall or change suddenly.
explain: «The wide base is stabilising the model tower.» The clue is wide base: a wide bottom stops a tower falling over, so stabilising must mean making it steady.
explain: «The extra wheels are stabilising my new bike.» Try your meaning in the sentence: the extra wheels are making my bike steady. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Stabilising can also describe a thing that helps keep something steady: «The stabilising wheels helped Ella ride without falling.» Here stabilising tells you what kind of wheels they are.
fact: Stabilising means making something steady and less likely to move, fall or change.
fact: Stabilising can describe a patient's health, prices or the weather becoming steady after a time of change.
fact: Stabilisers on a bike (UK) are called training wheels in the USA. They help young riders stay steady.
fact: A good check is to swap in steady or making steady. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the meaning.
exercise: «The wide base is stabilising the model so it stays upright.» What is stabilising doing? | Taking it apart | Blowing it over | *Making it steady | Painting it
exercise: «After the emergency, the patient's health is stabilising.» What does stabilising mean here? | Going on a long holiday | *Becoming steady after a time of change | Getting worse quickly | Shouting loudly
exercise: «The stabilising wheels helped Ella ride without falling.» Find and copy the word that describes the wheels. | without | falling | Ella | *stabilising
test: «Prices are stabilising after a year of big rises.» What does stabilising mean? | Rising faster and faster | *Becoming steady again | Disappearing | Being counted
test: Anna says stabilisers on a bike are training wheels. What do stabilisers help a rider do? | Stop pedalling | Ride faster than anyone | Fly over bumps | *Stay steady and not fall
exam: Which sentence uses stabilising as an adjective, describing a noun? | The tower is stabilising at last. | They stabilised the boat yesterday. | *«The stabilising effect kept the tower standing.» | He is stabilising the wobbly table with a book.
